+# SESSION_C2_DECISIONS
+
+## DEC-C2-001 — Pure-stdlib Chrome CDP instead of Playwright
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Implement a minimal WebSocket CDP client and interaction harness using installed Google Chrome only.
+- Context: Installs remain unauthorized; C1 dump-dom is insufficient for keyboard/focus execution proof.
+- Consequences: Real Runtime.evaluate + Input.dispatchKeyEvent evidence; not VoiceOver certification.
+
+## DEC-C2-002 — Code-tree SHA binding for receipts (v2)
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Seal `code_tree_sha256` over tracked product/code paths excluding SESSION_* and session-*-evidence. Prefer `--expect-code-tree` / `--recompute-code-tree` over chasing documentation tip SHAs.
+- Context: C1 noted self-referential commit loops when binding receipts to tip after return docs.
+- Consequences: FINAL_CODE_SHA can remain the immutable code commit; return packet docs may advance tip without invalidating code binding.
+
+## DEC-C2-003 — Filesystem fallback for code-tree digest
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: When `git ls-files` is empty/unavailable (git archive extract), walk CODE_PREFIXES on disk, skipping `__pycache__` and session evidence dirs.
+- Context: Clean-checkout proof failed with empty digest under archive trees.
+- Consequences: Clean temp trees can recompute `code_tree_sha256`; git worktrees still prefer tracked file set.
