+# SESSION_C_DECISIONS
+
+## DEC-C-001 — Browser strategy without package installs
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Do not install Playwright, browsers, or npm packages. Use installed Google Chrome headless (`--dump-dom`, `--screenshot`) plus Node mocked-DOM and static HTML/JS contract tests.
+- Context: Session forbids installs without approval; Playwright package absent despite ms-playwright cache.
+- Consequences: Real Chromium DOM dumps and screenshots are available; full AT (VoiceOver) and Playwright keyboard automation are not claimed.
+
+## DEC-C-002 — Post-date and post reserved-route policy remain documented gaps
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Do not invent generator enforcement for post `date` ISO format or post-slug membership in `RESERVED_ROUTES`. Keep/extend the Session 3 contract-gap tests as the formal encoding.
+- Context: Session 3 / PROJECT_HANDOFF chose document-not-invent; posts nest under `/journal/<slug>/` so top-level reserved collisions differ from app slug rules; `policy_effective_date` already validates ISO for apps.
+- Consequences: Invalid post dates still sort as opaque strings; reserved post slugs still load. Release dossier must list this limitation.
+
+## DEC-C-003 — Performance budgets from measured committed assets
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Budgets are ceilings derived from current committed `site/` sizes with modest headroom, not marketing performance claims.
+- Context: og.png ~1.0MiB and og-five-apps.png ~1.1MiB dominate; HTML/CSS/JS are comparatively small.
+- Consequences: Budget failures mean accidental bloat or unexpected assets, not Core Web Vitals proof.
+
+## DEC-C-004 — Generation only in Session C worktree or temp OUT
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Never run `generate_site.py` against live or integrate worktrees. Default OUT is this worktree `site/` or an explicit temp directory for tests/release_check.
+- Consequences: Integrate's dirty generated files remain as found.
+
+## DEC-C-005 — Lead owns shared generator/checkers; lanes own disjoint tests
+
+- Status: accepted
+- Decision: Lead integrates `scripts/release_check.py`, `scripts/validate_release_receipt.py`, `scripts/chrome_browser_probe.py`, and any `generate_site.py`/`check_site.py` patches. Workers (logical ownership) own only listed test files.
+- Consequences: Avoids conflicting edits to shared generator.
