+## Essential runbook (from PROJECT.md)
+
+### Release path
+1. Canonical source: `data/*`, `content/`, `scripts/generate_site.py` (+ themes/experiences).
+2. Regenerate committed `site/` from source (never hand-edit generated HTML for truth).
+3. Validate with repository tests, `check_site.py`, JS syntax checks, and existing C1–C4 harnesses / `local_verify.py`.
+4. Produce exact commit/artifact/hash + public route acceptance matrix including privacy/indexing and **complete WS-007 retained-route inventory**.
+5. Complete support runbook + **safe prior-artifact recovery rehearsal** before publication (WS-010).
+6. Obtain **concrete final release grant** naming reviewed commit/artifact, destination, and recovery plan (WEB-B03).
+7. Publish only through the existing selected GitHub Pages workflow on the authorized branch; capture Actions/deployment receipt and live HTTPS/route readback (WS-009) — **not authorized in this session**.
+
+### Mounted product preservation
+- WS-007 inventory (prior 12h evidence) shows live `/commercelint/`, `/bidetfit/`, `/machinecart/` while this candidate tip lacks mount sync scripts.
+- Generator `shutil.rmtree(OUT)` risk: regenerating+deploying without mount sync would omit/destroy mounts.
+- Stop condition: any retained mount absent/unexplained → **preserve-and-stop**; do not delete live routes.
+
+### Rollback
+- Preserve whole prior approved artifact and complete retained-route manifest (including CommerceLint and BidetFit).
+- Revert only the isolated authorized change or restore prior artifact via existing workflow under authority; independently read every retained public route after restore.
+- Never claim Apple binary rollback from website actions.
+- Credentials stay outside Git/Jira.
+
+### Outcome / 14-day (WS-011)
+- Compare permitted aggregate baseline vs post-release observations; keep small samples/confounders explicit.
+- Unavailable metrics are limitations, not zeros or fabrications.
+- One continue/change/pause decision; no implied redesign or contact authority.
+- **This session must not invent traffic/conversion data; 14-day closeout remains blocked without published release + permitted aggregates.**
+
+### Support / incidents
+- Actionable: website outage, false app availability, broken support/privacy routes, private-data exposure.
+- Preserve evidence and prior version; stop affected publication; smallest scoped correction; verify destination; record prevention.
+- Customer-facing responses require applicable communication grant.
+
+## Session constraints applied
+- No push / PR / merge / deploy / DNS / publication.
+- No trackers/cookies/remote analytics scripts added.
