+<header class="product-nav"><a class="product-wordmark" href="../../index.html">Priyansh Chordia <span>· iOS</span></a><nav aria-label="Product"><a href="../../index.html#work">Products</a><a href="#top">Mala</a><a href="#waitlist">Join waitlist</a></nav></header>
+<div id="top"><section class="product-hero"><div><p class="product-kicker">Mala</p><h1>A quiet digital mala.</h1><p class="product-hero-body">Keep your place. Feel each count. Finish without looking. One tap advances one bead — and the count survives a phone call, a locked screen, or the rest of the day.</p><p class="product-hero-note">In TestFlight beta — not on the App Store yet. No account, advertising, analytics, tracking, or developer-operated service. Practice information stays in the app's local storage.</p><div class="product-actions"><a class="product-button" href="#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a><a href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><div class="product-motif" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div></section>
+<section class="product-shots"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>The app</p><h2>Five screens. That is the whole app.</h2></div><div class="product-shots-grid"><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Practice surface screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Practice surface</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Round complete screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Round complete</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Personal label screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Personal label</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Mala styles screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Mala styles</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="History screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>History</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+<section class="product-benefits"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Why it exists</p><h2>Three things a physical mala already does well.</h2></div><div class="product-triad"><article><span>01</span><h3>Count by feel</h3><p>A large practice surface and restrained feedback keep attention on the repetition.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Resume naturally</h3><p>An interrupted round can continue without turning practice into a productivity task.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Make it yours</h3><p>Private labels, multiple mala styles, and local history support a personal ritual.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="how-it-works" class="product-steps"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>How it works</p><h2>Four steps, then you can put the screen away.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Choose a round and an optional private label.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Tap through each repetition at your own pace.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Complete the round and keep the history on your device.</p></li></ol></section>
+<section class="product-trust"><div><p>Privacy and trust</p><h2>There is no server to send anything to.</h2><p>No account, advertising, analytics, tracking, or developer-operated service. Practice information stays in the app's local storage.</p><div class="product-legal-links"><a href="../../apps/mala/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="../../apps/mala/support/">Support</a></div></div><aside><p>Honest boundary</p><strong>Mala supports practice; it does not provide religious instruction, health guidance, or social features.</strong></aside></section>
+<section class="product-features"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Feature highlights</p><h2>Everything in the beta build.</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Choose a round size</dt><dd>01</dd></div><div><dt>Name it, or don't</dt><dd>02</dd></div><div><dt>Tap to advance</dt><dd>03</dd></div><div><dt>Finish without looking</dt><dd>04</dd></div><div><dt>No account or cloud backend</dt><dd>05</dd></div><div><dt>TestFlight builds expire</dt><dd>06</dd></div></dl></section>
+<section class="product-fit"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Who the beta is for</p><h2>Useful to a few people. Not to everyone.</h2></div><div><article><h3>A good fit if you</h3><p>For anyone who wants a simple digital mala without feeds, accounts, or performative streaks.</p></article><article><h3>Mala is deliberately not</h3><p>Mala supports practice; it does not provide religious instruction, health guidance, or social features.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="waitlist" class="product-waitlist"><div><p>Waitlist</p><h2>Ask for a TestFlight invitation.</h2><p>No account is created. Your email is stored only to send Mala beta invitations.</p></div><form data-waitlist="" data-app-name="Mala" action="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Mala%20beta" method="post"><label for="waitlist-email-mala">Email address <em>(required)</em><input id="waitlist-email-mala" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-mala" required=""></label><label>First name <em>(optional)</em><input type="text" name="first_name" autocomplete="given-name"></label><label>Device and iOS version, or what you want to test <em>(optional)</em><textarea name="device" aria-describedby="device-hint"></textarea><small id="device-hint">Helps prioritise invitations across devices. Leave blank if you would rather not say.</small></label><label class="product-consent"><input id="waitlist-consent-mala" type="checkbox" name="consent" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-mala" required=""> Email me about TestFlight access and occasional updates for Mala. I can unsubscribe at any time.</label><button class="product-button" type="submit">Join the Mala waitlist</button><p id="waitlist-status-mala" class="waitlist-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"></p><p class="waitlist-fallback">The signup service is not connected yet. Email <a href="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Mala%20beta">support@priyanshchordia.com</a> with the subject “Mala beta” and you will be added by hand.</p></form></section>
+<section class="product-faq"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Questions and limits</p><h2>What Mala does, and what it will not do.</h2></div><details><summary>Can I download Mala from the App Store?</summary><p>No. Mala is in TestFlight beta and is not available on the App Store yet.</p></details><details><summary>How soon will I get an invitation?</summary><p>Invitations are sent in small groups as testing capacity opens. There is no queue position or promised timeline.</p></details><details><summary>What do you do with my email address?</summary><p>It is used only to send beta invitations and occasional updates. You can ask to be removed at any time.</p></details><div class="product-limits"><p>Honest limitations</p><strong>Mala supports practice; it does not provide religious instruction, health guidance, or social features.</strong></div></section>
