+<title>Anjali — priyanshchordia.com</title><link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%2032%2032'%3E%3Crect%20width='32'%20height='32'%20rx='7'%20fill='%23141414'/%3E%3Ccircle%20cx='16'%20cy='16'%20r='6'%20fill='%23d7ff4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" type="image/svg+xml">
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css?v=9883ddb311"></head>
+<body class="product-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="wrap">
+<header class="top"><div class="left">
+
+<a class="brand" href="../../index.html">P/C <span class="status" aria-hidden="true">●</span></a></div>
+<nav aria-label="Primary"><a class="active" aria-current="page" href="../../index.html#work">Work</a><a href="../../apps/">App URLs</a><a href="../../journal/">Journal</a></nav></header>
+<main id="main"><article class="product-system product-system--anjali" data-app="anjali">
+<header class="product-nav"><a class="product-wordmark" href="../../index.html">Priyansh Chordia <span>· iOS</span></a><nav aria-label="Product"><a href="../../index.html#work">Products</a><a href="#top">Anjali</a><a href="#waitlist">Join waitlist</a></nav></header>
+<div id="top"><section class="product-hero"><div><p class="product-kicker">Anjali</p><h1>A sacred pause, not a session.</h1><p class="product-hero-body">One short prayer for the moment you are in — with the Devanagari, a transliteration, and a plain-English meaning on the same screen. Then you close the app.</p><p class="product-hero-note">In TestFlight beta — not on the App Store yet. No account, backend, analytics, advertising, tracking, third-party SDKs, or purchases. Preferences and activity remain on-device.</p><div class="product-actions"><a class="product-button" href="#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a><a href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><div class="product-motif" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div></section>
+<section class="product-shots"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>The app</p><h2>One prayer, held on one screen.</h2></div><div class="product-shots-grid"><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Prayer detail screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Prayer detail</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Browse by moment screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Browse by moment</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Chant or silent screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Chant or silent</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+<section class="product-benefits"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Why it exists</p><h2>Built to be closed after the prayer.</h2></div><div class="product-triad"><article><span>01</span><h3>Brief by design</h3><p>Open Anjali, meet one focused prayer, and return to your day.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Available offline</h3><p>Bundled content works without an account or developer-operated service.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Return gently</h3><p>Optional local reminders and favorites help make room for the moments that matter.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="how-it-works" class="product-steps"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>How it works</p><h2>Three steps, then put it down.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Choose the moment you are in.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Read or chant one short prayer at your own pace.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Save what matters or close the app when the pause is complete.</p></li></ol></section>
+<section class="product-trust"><div><p>Privacy and trust</p><h2>A prayer is not an event to be logged.</h2><p>No account, backend, analytics, advertising, tracking, third-party SDKs, or purchases. Preferences and activity remain on-device.</p><div class="product-legal-links"><a href="../../apps/anjali/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="../../apps/anjali/support/">Support</a></div></div><aside><p>Honest boundary</p><strong>Current Chant practice is self-led and silent. Anjali does not claim religious authority and is not a puja guide.</strong></aside></section>
+<section class="product-features"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Feature highlights</p><h2>Everything in the beta build.</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Short on purpose</dt><dd>01</dd></div><div><dt>Read it three ways</dt><dd>02</dd></div><div><dt>Browse by moment</dt><dd>03</dd></div><div><dt>Chant or silent</dt><dd>04</dd></div><div><dt>Offline and accountless</dt><dd>05</dd></div><div><dt>No recorded audio</dt><dd>06</dd></div></dl></section>
+<section class="product-fit"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Who the beta is for</p><h2>A small app for a small moment.</h2></div><div><article><h3>A good fit if you</h3><p>For people who want a brief, private moment of Hindu prayer without opening a feed or starting a long session.</p></article><article><h3>Anjali is deliberately not</h3><p>Current Chant practice is self-led and silent. Anjali does not claim religious authority and is not a puja guide.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="waitlist" class="product-waitlist"><div><p>Waitlist</p><h2>Ask for a TestFlight invitation.</h2><p>No account is created. Your email is stored only to send Anjali beta invitations.</p></div><form data-waitlist="" data-app-name="Anjali" action="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Anjali%20beta" method="post" novalidate=""><label for="waitlist-email-anjali">Email address <em>(required)</em><input id="waitlist-email-anjali" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-anjali" required=""></label><label>First name <em>(optional)</em><input type="text" name="first_name" autocomplete="given-name"></label><label>Device and iOS version, or what you want to test <em>(optional)</em><textarea name="device" aria-describedby="device-hint"></textarea><small id="device-hint">Helps prioritise invitations across devices. Leave blank if you would rather not say.</small></label><label class="product-consent"><input id="waitlist-consent-anjali" type="checkbox" name="consent" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-anjali" required=""> Email me about TestFlight access and occasional updates for Anjali. I can unsubscribe at any time.</label><button class="product-button" type="submit">Join the Anjali waitlist</button><p id="waitlist-status-anjali" class="waitlist-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"></p><p class="waitlist-fallback">The signup service is not connected yet. Email <a href="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Anjali%20beta">support@priyanshchordia.com</a> with the subject “Anjali beta” and you will be added by hand.</p></form></section>
+<section class="product-faq"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Questions and limits</p><h2>Asked, and answered honestly.</h2></div><details><summary>Can I download Anjali from the App Store?</summary><p>No. Anjali is in TestFlight beta and is not available on the App Store yet.</p></details><details><summary>How soon will I get an invitation?</summary><p>Invitations are sent in small groups as testing capacity opens. There is no queue position or promised timeline.</p></details><details><summary>What do you do with my email address?</summary><p>It is used only to send beta invitations and occasional updates. You can ask to be removed at any time.</p></details><div class="product-limits"><p>Honest limitations</p><strong>Current Chant practice is self-led and silent. Anjali does not claim religious authority and is not a puja guide.</strong></div></section>
+<footer class="product-footer"><p>More from this portfolio</p><h2>Independent iOS apps, built one at a time.</h2><div><a href="../../apps/anjali/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="../../apps/anjali/support/">Support</a><a href="../../index.html#work">All products</a><a href="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com">support@priyanshchordia.com</a></div><small>© 2026 Priyansh Chordia. Anjali is in TestFlight beta and is not available on the App Store.</small></footer></div></article></main>
