+<title>Roam — priyanshchordia.com</title><link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%2032%2032'%3E%3Crect%20width='32'%20height='32'%20rx='7'%20fill='%23141414'/%3E%3Ccircle%20cx='16'%20cy='16'%20r='6'%20fill='%23d7ff4a'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" type="image/svg+xml">
+<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css?v=9883ddb311"></head>
+<body class="product-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><div class="wrap">
+<header class="top"><div class="left">
+
+<a class="brand" href="../../index.html">P/C <span class="status" aria-hidden="true">●</span></a></div>
+<nav aria-label="Primary"><a class="active" aria-current="page" href="../../index.html#work">Work</a><a href="../../apps/">App URLs</a><a href="../../journal/">Journal</a></nav></header>
+<main id="main"><article class="product-system product-system--roam" data-app="roam">
+<header class="product-nav"><a class="product-wordmark" href="../../index.html">Priyansh Chordia <span>· iOS</span></a><nav aria-label="Product"><a href="../../index.html#work">Products</a><a href="#top">Roam</a><a href="#waitlist">Join waitlist</a></nav></header>
+<div id="top"><section class="product-hero"><div><p class="product-kicker">Roam</p><h1>Your travels, coloured in.</h1><p class="product-hero-body">A private map of the places you have explored. Switch tracking on and Roam fills in supported U.S. Census ZIP Code Areas as you move. Anywhere else in the world, add countries and cities by hand.</p><p class="product-hero-note">In TestFlight beta — not on the App Store yet. No Roam account, developer cloud, advertising, or third-party analytics. Apple services process what MapKit, Core Location, and StoreKit require.</p><div class="product-actions"><a class="product-button" href="#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a><a href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div><div class="product-motif" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div></section>
+<section class="product-shots"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>The app</p><h2>The same map, at six levels of zoom.</h2></div><div class="product-shots-grid"><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Coverage map screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Coverage map</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Location choice screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Location choice</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Saved places screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Saved places</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="product-shot" aria-label="Export summary screenshot placeholder"><span>Screenshot pending</span></div><figcaption>Export summary</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+<section class="product-benefits"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Why it exists</p><h2>Detailed enough to be interesting. Private enough to keep.</h2></div><div class="product-triad"><article><span>01</span><h3>Watch coverage grow</h3><p>Visited ZIP Code Areas and countries accumulate into a map that feels tangible.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Choose permission deliberately</h3><p>A staged location flow explains foreground and background access before you opt in.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Share the summary</h3><p>Create aggregate coverage cards or export your data when you choose.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="how-it-works" class="product-steps"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>How it works</p><h2>Four steps, and one of them is optional.</h2></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Choose how much location access to grant.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Travel while Roam matches samples against bundled geographic boundaries.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Review, export, or share aggregate coverage on your terms.</p></li></ol></section>
+<section class="product-trust"><div><p>Privacy and trust</p><h2>Location history is the most sensitive data you own.</h2><p>No Roam account, developer cloud, advertising, or third-party analytics. Apple services process what MapKit, Core Location, and StoreKit require.</p><div class="product-legal-links"><a href="../../apps/roam/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="../../apps/roam/support/">Support</a></div></div><aside><p>Honest boundary</p><strong>ZIP Code Areas are Census approximations, not postal delivery boundaries. Automatic tracking requires location permission.</strong></aside></section>
+<section class="product-features"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Feature highlights</p><h2>Everything in the beta build.</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Decide about tracking</dt><dd>01</dd></div><div><dt>Travel</dt><dd>02</dd></div><div><dt>Add the rest by hand</dt><dd>03</dd></div><div><dt>Keep control of it</dt><dd>04</dd></div><div><dt>Export and delete</dt><dd>05</dd></div><div><dt>Synthetic map data in the preview</dt><dd>06</dd></div></dl></section>
+<section class="product-fit"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Who the beta is for</p><h2>Map people, mostly.</h2></div><div><article><h3>A good fit if you</h3><p>For curious travelers who want a personal coverage map without handing their saved history to a travel social network.</p></article><article><h3>Roam is deliberately not</h3><p>ZIP Code Areas are Census approximations, not postal delivery boundaries. Automatic tracking requires location permission.</p></article></div></section>
+<section id="waitlist" class="product-waitlist"><div><p>Waitlist</p><h2>Ask for a TestFlight invitation.</h2><p>No account is created. Your email is stored only to send Roam beta invitations.</p></div><form data-waitlist="" data-app-name="Roam" action="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Roam%20beta" method="post" novalidate=""><label for="waitlist-email-roam">Email address <em>(required)</em><input id="waitlist-email-roam" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-roam" required=""></label><label>First name <em>(optional)</em><input type="text" name="first_name" autocomplete="given-name"></label><label>Device and iOS version, or what you want to test <em>(optional)</em><textarea name="device" aria-describedby="device-hint"></textarea><small id="device-hint">Helps prioritise invitations across devices. Leave blank if you would rather not say.</small></label><label class="product-consent"><input id="waitlist-consent-roam" type="checkbox" name="consent" aria-describedby="waitlist-status-roam" required=""> Email me about TestFlight access and occasional updates for Roam. I can unsubscribe at any time.</label><button class="product-button" type="submit">Join the Roam waitlist</button><p id="waitlist-status-roam" class="waitlist-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1"></p><p class="waitlist-fallback">The signup service is not connected yet. Email <a href="mailto:support@priyanshchordia.com?subject=Roam%20beta">support@priyanshchordia.com</a> with the subject “Roam beta” and you will be added by hand.</p></form></section>
+<section class="product-faq"><div class="product-section-heading"><p>Questions and limits</p><h2>The precise answers.</h2></div><details><summary>Can I download Roam from the App Store?</summary><p>No. Roam is in TestFlight beta and is not available on the App Store yet.</p></details><details><summary>How soon will I get an invitation?</summary><p>Invitations are sent in small groups as testing capacity opens. There is no queue position or promised timeline.</p></details><details><summary>What do you do with my email address?</summary><p>It is used only to send beta invitations and occasional updates. You can ask to be removed at any time.</p></details><div class="product-limits"><p>Honest limitations</p><strong>ZIP Code Areas are Census approximations, not postal delivery boundaries. Automatic tracking requires location permission.</strong></div></section>
