+# Accessibility and UX Independent Review — Session C4
+
+- **Reviewer Model:** Gemini 3.7 Flash (Independent Accessibility/UX Reviewer subagent)
+- **Checkpoint SHA Reviewed:** `f8c87ab15c398402b0c04b4f96e85d28df6237f7`
+- **Review Date:** 2026-09-07
+- **Verdict:** **Approve with notes**
+
+---
+
+## Executive Summary
+
+An independent accessibility and UX review was conducted on Session C4 of `priyanshchordia.com` at checkpoint SHA `f8c87ab15c398402b0c04b4f96e85d28df6237f7`.
+
+The evaluation focused on:
+1. `scripts/a11y_depth_harness.py` (C4 Lane 2: contrast proxies, zoom/reflow, live regions, positive tabindex, duplicate IDs, ARIA reference integrity)
+2. `scripts/chrome_browser_matrix_harness.py` (C4 Lane 1: 22 interactive routes across keyboard, pointer, skip link activation, history recovery, reload, fragments, emulated media, storage edge cases, waitlist submissions, offline resilience)
+3. `scripts/chrome_keyboard_a11y_harness.py` (C3/C4 keyboard audit: 137 test cases across 22 routes, skip visibility, activation evidence, experience theme dialog traps, Escape handling, reduced motion)
+4. `scripts/semantic_a11y_harness.py` (Semantic HTML/ARIA static analysis, landmark counts, heading hierarchies, form control accessible names, live CDP waitlist error focus)
+5. `scripts/visual_depth_harness.py` (C4 Lane 8: 12 routes across desktop, tablet, and mobile viewports, structural layout signals, overflow detection, broken image detection, bounded screenshots)
+6. Supporting test suites (`tests/test_a11y_depth.py`, `tests/test_browser_matrix.py`, `tests/test_visual_depth.py`, `tests/test_semantic_a11y.py`, `tests/test_browser_a11y_contracts.py`, `tests/experiences_a11y.test.cjs`, `tests/waitlist.test.cjs`, `tests/test_waitlist_markup.py`)
+7. Evidence artifacts in `session-c4-evidence/a11y-depth`, `session-c4-evidence/browser-matrix`, and `session-c4-evidence/visual`.
+
+**Overall Assessment:**
+The implementation exhibits high engineering discipline. Boundaries are scrupulously honest: nowhere is assistive-technology (AT) or VoiceOver certification claimed. Semantic HTML structure, keyboard focus management, modal dialog trapping, dynamic skip links, and accessible form error states are implemented cleanly with stdlib and lightweight CDP automation. Minor limitations in single-element contrast proxy sampling and CSS zoom mechanics are noted below with disposition recommendations.
+
+---
+
+## Verdict and Findings Summary
+
+| # | Sev | Area | Summary | Disposition Recommendation |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **F-01** | Low | Contrast Proxy | `a11y_depth_harness.py` samples only the primary text element on the homepage under the active theme against `body.backgroundColor`. | **Accept as C4 proxy**. For future sessions, consider a multi-theme contrast matrix covering secondary text classes (`.resource-note`, `.policy-date`, `.facts dt`). |
+| **F-02** | Low | Zoom vs Reflow | `home.zoom_200_main_present` tests `html.style.zoom = '200%'` (which alters Chromium CSS coordinates rather than device pixel ratio) as a presence check. | **Accept with note**. The harness treats this purely as a soft presence signal, while `product.narrow_320_main` and `visual_depth_harness.py` (320px/375px viewports) provide true WCAG 1.4.10 reflow verification. |
+| **F-03** | Low | Tab Cycle Depth | `tab_order_no_trap` samples the first 10–16 tab stops, which verifies initial navigation and trap-absence, but does not exhaustively traverse deep catalog pages. | **Accept**. 10–16 tabs is sufficient for loopback trap detection. Specialized experience interactions (e.g. arrow keys in Cabinet, modal trapping in Unknown Signal) are tested via dedicated contract and live suites. |
+| **F-04** | Info | Skip Link & Focus UX | Dynamic skip link rebinding (`installExperienceSkip` / `restorePageSkip`), off-screen to on-screen transition, and `pageSkip.inert` during modal dialogs work seamlessly. | **Commend**. Clean UX and accessible focus restoration across experience lifecycle switches. |
+| **F-05** | Info | Waitlist Error UX | `waitlist.js` provides dynamic `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby` error associations, `status.focus()`, and maintains honest unavailable fallbacks without false success claims. | **Commend**. Complies with WCAG 3.3.1 (Error Identification), 3.3.2 (Labels/Instructions), and 3.3.3 (Error Suggestion). |
+| **F-06** | Info | Non-AT Boundaries | All harnesses, summaries, and receipts explicitly state they provide local CDP browser evidence and do NOT constitute VoiceOver / AT certification. | **Commend**. Clear boundary discipline prevents false confidence. |
+
+---
+
+## Detailed Evaluation by Focus Area
+
+### 1. Accessibility Depth Harness (`scripts/a11y_depth_harness.py`)
+- **Static Parser (`DepthParser`):**
+  - Accurately identifies `html[lang]`, landmarks (`main`, `nav`, `header`, `footer`, `aside`, and ARIA landmark roles), heading outlines, duplicate IDs, positive tabindex values, and ARIA reference validity (`aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`, `aria-controls`, `aria-owns`).
+  - Verifies waitlist status regions and `tabindex="-1"` on product pages.
+  - Successfully validated all 22 interactive HTML routes without syntax errors or false positives.
+- **Live CDP Signals:**
+  - `home.tab_cycle_no_obvious_trap`: Detects element repetition streaks (>=3 consecutive identical elements) to flag keyboard traps.
+  - `home.contrast_proxy_body_text`: Computes standard relative luminance (\(L = 0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B\)) and contrast ratio (\((L_1 + 0.05)/(L_2 + 0.05)\)). Evaluates computed colors cleanly.
+  - `product.narrow_320_main`: Tests 320px width reflow, verifying `<main>` presence and no horizontal overflow.
+  - `home.reduced_motion_skip_first_tab`: Verifies that under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, the keyboard skip link remains the first focusable element.
+
+### 2. Chrome Browser Matrix Harness (`scripts/chrome_browser_matrix_harness.py`)
+- **Coverage:**
+  - Evaluates all 22 interactive HTML routes across 10 distinct audit categories.
+  - Tests page load stability, skip link first-tab focus, skip link activation to `#main` / `#xp-main`, linear tab order without traps, page reload preservation, URL fragment navigation (`#main`), and browser history back/forward focus recovery.
+- **Edge-Case Probes:**
+  - Pointer activation on skip link (`audit_route_pointer`): Validates that after Tab reveals the skip link, pointer clicks dispatching via CDP `Input.dispatchMouseEvent` successfully navigate to the target main element.
+  - Storage edge cases (`audit_storage_edges`): Verifies theme switcher stability when `localStorage` methods throw or contain corrupted JSON strings.
+  - Malformed query strings (`audit_weird_query`): Probes `%ZZ`, null bytes, and script injection strings without runtime errors.
+  - Emulated media (`audit_emulated_media`): Verifies reduced motion, dark scheme, and light scheme matchMedia queries.
+  - Waitlist submission & offline resilience (`audit_waitlist`, `audit_offline_brief`): Probes repeated submissions and offline network conditions (`Network.emulateNetworkConditions`), ensuring no permanent crash and zero false success claims.
+
+### 3. Chrome Keyboard Accessibility Harness (`scripts/chrome_keyboard_a11y_harness.py`)
+- **Coverage & Robustness:**
+  - 137 test cases executed across 22 interactive routes.
+  - Skip link visibility check (`skip_first_tab_visible`) requires either on-screen bounding rect (`left >= 0` and `width > 0`) or active CSS focus indicators (`outlineStyle != 'none'` or `boxShadow != 'none'`).
+  - Skip target activation (`skip_target`) requires real focus change or URL hash update, rejecting static tabindex artifacts.
+  - Experience dialogs (`audit_home_experience_dialogs`): Sweeps Overworld, Unknown Signal, Parallel, and Cabinet themes, triggering interactive dialogs and asserting clean Escape key closure.
+
+### 4. Semantic Accessibility Harness (`scripts/semantic_a11y_harness.py`)
+- **Semantic Structure & Forms:**
+  - Validates landmark uniqueness (exactly 1 `<main>` per page), accessible naming on `<nav>` elements, heading level sequence (no skips > 1 level), explicit/wrapped input label associations, and `<img>` `alt` attributes.
+  - Live status focus test (`run_live_waitlist_status_focus`): Simulates empty waitlist form submission on `/products/mala/` and proves via CDP that focus shifts to the status container (`document.activeElement === status`), `aria-invalid="true"` is assigned to the input, and `aria-describedby` correctly connects the error text.
+
+### 5. Visual Depth Harness (`scripts/visual_depth_harness.py`)
+- **Layout & Responsiveness:**
+  - 36 entries spanning 12 representative routes across desktop (1280x800), tablet (768x1024), and mobile (375x812) viewports.
+  - Checks `<main>` presence, non-empty content lengths, zero broken images (`naturalWidth === 0`), and mobile horizontal overflow limits.
+  - Bounded screenshot capability (PNG size limit of 1.5 MB with SHA256 hashing) prevents evidence bloat.
+
+---
+
+## Detailed Findings and Disposition Notes
+
+### Finding F-01: Contrast Proxy Scope and Theme Sampling
+- **Severity:** Low (Minor / Informational)
+- **Observed Behavior:** `a11y_depth_harness.py` inspects the computed `color` of the first matching heading or paragraph on the home page and checks contrast against `document.body.backgroundColor`. It applies a threshold of `3.0` as a proxy floor.
+- **Risk Analysis:** Some theme variations (e.g. high-saturation or specialized palettes) or secondary elements (such as `.policy-date`, `.resource-note`, or `.fact dt`) are not individually measured by this single probe.
+- **Disposition:** **Accept as C4 proxy**. The harness explicitly notes that this is a local proxy check and not formal certification.
+- **Future Recommendation:** In a future session, implement a multi-theme contrast sweep that inspects foreground/background pairs for declared CSS theme custom properties.
+
+### Finding F-02: Chromium CSS Zoom Emulation vs Device Reflow
+- **Severity:** Low (Minor / Informational)
+- **Observed Behavior:** `home.zoom_200_main_present` applies `html.style.zoom = '200%'` and checks `document.body.scrollWidth`. In Chromium, CSS `zoom` on the root element modifies layout coordinates rather than simulating native browser zoom (where the viewport dimensions shrink).
+- **Risk Analysis:** Minimal, because the harness only uses this as a soft signal for `<main>` presence.
+- **Disposition:** **Accept with notes**. Full WCAG 1.4.10 Reflow is verified by `product.narrow_320_main` (320px viewport) and `visual_depth_harness.py` (375px mobile viewport), both of which confirm zero unwanted horizontal overflow.
+
+### Finding F-03: Fixed Tab Cycle Depth on Deep Routes
+- **Severity:** Low (Minor)
+- **Observed Behavior:** Keyboard trap probes tab 10 to 16 times from the top of the page. On longer catalog pages, 16 tabs does not reach footer links.
+- **Risk Analysis:** Low. The primary objective of the tab cycle harness is to detect immediate keyboard traps, circular focus loops, and verify the skip link sequence.
+- **Disposition:** **Accept**. Specialized interactive elements (e.g., custom slider in Unknown Signal, product cards in Cabinet, dialog modals in Overworld) are independently exercised by unit contract tests and matrix probes.
+
+### Finding F-04: Dynamic Skip Link & Experience Focus Lifecycle
+- **Severity:** Positive / Informational
+- **Observed Behavior:** When interactive experiences mount in `#xp`, `installExperienceSkip()` updates the skip link target to `#xp-main` and label to `"Skip to experience"`. During modal dialog states, `pageSkip` is marked `inert` and `hidden` to prevent focus escaping. When experiences tear down, `restorePageSkip()` cleanly restores `"Skip to content"` pointing to `#main`.
+- **Disposition:** **Approved**. Demonstrates robust focus management across dynamic UI states.
+
+### Finding F-05: Accessible Form Validation and Fallback UX
+- **Severity:** Positive / Informational
+- **Observed Behavior:** Product waitlist forms combine explicit labels, dynamic `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby` associations, polite live region announcements, and direct focus transfer (`status.focus()`). Fallback copy is honest and helpful ("The signup form is unavailable right now... added by hand").
+- **Disposition:** **Approved**. Adheres to accessible UX patterns and prevents user confusion.
+
+### Finding F-06: Strict Non-Assistive-Technology Certification Boundaries
+- **Severity:** Positive / Informational
+- **Observed Behavior:** All test outputs, JSON evidence files, and harness docstrings clearly disclaim VoiceOver / AT certification, characterizing results accurately as local Chrome CDP automation evidence.
+- **Disposition:** **Approved**. Complies fully with project governance rules.
+
+---
+
+## Residual Risks and Limitations
+
+1. **No Screen Reader / Assistive Technology Certification:**
+   Automated CDP keyboard events and DOM attribute checks cannot verify screen reader announcements across macOS VoiceOver, Windows NVDA/JAWS, or iOS VoiceOver. Manual AT validation remains necessary for formal compliance.
+2. **Synthesized Events vs Native OS Focus:**
+   CDP `Input.dispatchKeyEvent` simulates key events inside Chromium, but does not replicate platform-level focus modes (e.g. macOS Safari Full Keyboard Access).
+3. **Receipt Sealing:**
+   Any modification to scripts, tests, or markup requires re-executing `local_verify.py` to seal and validate the release receipt.
+
+---
+
+## Final Recommendation
+
+**Verdict: Approve with notes.**
+
+The accessibility and UX harnesses, test suites, and generated evidence in Session C4 provide high-confidence, well-bounded verification across all 22 interactive routes. No blockers or regressions were identified. No product code changes are required.
